# Pre-deploy verification

Vercel production deploys run `next build`, which type-checks the whole app. `next dev` does not. Failed production deploys from this repo have almost always been TypeScript errors pushed straight to `main`.

## Required before commit or push

1. Run `npm run typecheck` (same as CI: `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.ci.json`).
2. If you changed tests, Stripe/billing, or i18n keys, also run `npm test`.
3. If either command fails: fix the errors, re-run until green, then commit/push.
4. Never push a red typecheck. Never use `--no-verify` on commit or push.

`npm run verify` runs typecheck then tests. A green `next dev` compile is not deploy-ready.
